---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CITIES, SOURCE } from "../lib/cost-of-living.js";
import checks from "../../data/source-checks.json";

const byName = [...CITIES].sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const readOn = checks.sources["bea-rpp"]?.lastVerified;
const date = iso => {
  if (typeof iso !== "string" || !/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(iso)) return "an unknown date";
  const [year, month, day] = iso.split("-").map(Number);
  return new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", { dateStyle: "long", timeZone: "UTC" }).format(new Date(Date.UTC(year, month - 1, day)));
};
---
<Layout
  title="Cost of Living Comparison Between US Cities — Relocation Cost"
  description="Compare the overall price level of two US metro areas using the Bureau of Economic Analysis Regional Price Parities, and see what the same average spending would cost in the other city."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-700">Cost of living</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Compare prices between two cities</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">Moving costs are one number; the price level where you land is another. Pick two of the calculator's cities to see how their overall prices compare, using the federal government's regional price index for {SOURCE.year}. It describes the average household's spending, not yours.</p>

    <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm sm:p-6" aria-labelledby="compare-heading">
      <h2 id="compare-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold">Compare two cities</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Moving from
          <select id="fromCity" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-400 bg-white p-3 text-base font-normal">
            {byName.map(city => <option value={city.slug}>{city.name}, {city.state}</option>)}
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Moving to
          <select id="toCity" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-400 bg-white p-3 text-base font-normal">
            {byName.map(city => <option value={city.slug} selected={city.slug === "austin"}>{city.name}, {city.state}</option>)}
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <label class="mt-4 block text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Your current monthly spending, in US dollars (optional)
        <input id="spending" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="50" placeholder="for example 4000" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-400 bg-white p-3 text-base font-normal sm:max-w-xs" />
      </label>
      <div id="result" class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-800" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <p id="resultSentence" class="text-base font-semibold"></p>
        <p id="resultSpending" class="mt-2" hidden></p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-600">The result uses one all-items index per metro area. Nothing you type leaves your browser.</p>
    </section>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">How to read this</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li>The index compares each metro area's overall price level with the U.S. average of 100. A value of 110 means prices are about 10% above the national average.</li>
      <li>It is built from a typical consumer's spending across many categories, with housing rents measured from the American Community Survey. A household that spends very differently, for example one that owns its home outright, will see a different gap.</li>
      <li>Some categories use national prices, so the index understates how much those areas differ.</li>
      <li>The figures are for {SOURCE.year}, the latest year in this metropolitan table, and prices have moved since. Treat the result as a first comparison, then check real rents and quotes for the neighborhoods you are considering.</li>
      <li>It does not include the cost of the move itself. For that, use the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/calculator/">moving cost calculator</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">All cities, lowest to highest price level</h2>
    <div tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table" class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[30rem] text-left text-sm leading-6">
        <caption class="sr-only">Price index by metropolitan area, U.S. average equals 100</caption>
        <thead class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">City</th>
            <th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">Metropolitan area</th>
            <th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">Index</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-slate-600">
          {CITIES.map(city => (
            <tr class="border-b border-slate-100 last:border-0">
              <th scope="row" class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">{city.name}, {city.state}</th>
              <td class="p-4">{city.metro}</td>
              <td class="p-4">{city.rpp.toFixed(1)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Source</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis, <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={SOURCE.url} rel="noopener">Table 4, Regional Price Parities by Metropolitan Area, {SOURCE.year}</a> (all-items column). Method: <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={SOURCE.methodologyUrl} rel="noopener">BEA methodology for Regional Price Parities</a>. The values were read from the table on {date(readOn)} and cross-checked against the table's own deflator column. The table is a yearly federal release, so the page is reviewed by hand and flagged for review when it is about five months old.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Next: <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/calculator/">estimate the cost of the move</a>, then <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/budget-tracker/">track the budget</a>.</p>
  </article>
  <script src="../scripts/cost-of-living.js"></script>
</Layout>
